{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>It appears to me</b> — two instances with the word דין (i.e., נראה לי דין), and the other (instance) from afar. 'It appears to me' (ה' נראה לי) — this is what the Sages said: even a Torah scholar expert in nega'im must not say 'nega' (נגע) but only 'like a nega' (כנגע). And this is 'from afar it appears' — he takes up the matter from afar and does not rule definitively to say 'nega.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:25.650668298Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}